    "figcap": "World aid from the seventeen biggest donors, 2024 to 2026, and the routes UNDP's Pacific office is sketching for the region after it. Donor figures from the Council on Foreign Relations, 2025; scenarios from UNDP Pacific, 2025.",
    "teaser": "The seventeen biggest donors gave 198.7 billion dollars in 2024. The projection for 2026 is 151.6 billion. UNDP's Pacific office has started planning for a region that runs on something other than aid.",
    "body": "The era in which aid grew steadily is over. The seventeen biggest donors gave 198.7 billion US dollars in 2024, and flows are projected to fall to about 151.6 billion in 2026, nearly 29 percent below 2023, with USAID closed and several European donors cutting for a second year running. What remains is increasingly shaped by geopolitical competition rather than need alone. UNDP's Pacific office is already sketching scenarios for a post-aid region, from sovereign funds, domestic revenue, and diaspora bonds to a fragmented future where power plays come before people. For small islands the question is shifting from how much aid arrives to who decides what it is for.",
