    "title": "The price of sending money home",
    "art": "<svg viewBox='0 0 110 110' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' aria-hidden='true'><circle cx='52' cy='58' r='34' fill='#FFCC00' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='2.6'/><circle cx='80' cy='32' r='17' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='50' y='70' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='32' fill='#993C1D'>$</text><text x='86' y='26' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='13' fill='#993C1D'>%</text></svg>",
    "fig": "<svg viewBox='0 0 760 362' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' role='img' aria-label='Sending 200 US dollars home costs about 6 per cent on average against a global target of 3 per cent, with a new 1 per cent United States excise from January 2026.'><rect width='760' height='362' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='36' y='34' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='9.5' letter-spacing='1.5' fill='#3D5560'>COST OF SENDING 200 US DOLLARS HOME, PER CENT OF THE AMOUNT</text><text x='36' y='68' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0B2530'>What it costs on average</text><rect x='250' y='55' width='274.3' height='20' rx='2' fill='#E2664A' fill-opacity='0.9' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='534.3' y='69' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#993C1D'>about 6 per cent</text><text x='36' y='112' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0B2530'>The global target</text><rect x='250' y='99' width='137.1' height='20' rx='2' fill='#1C8C9B' fill-opacity='0.9' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='397.1' y='113' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0E4D5C'>3 per cent</text><text x='250' y='148' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>Cash and bank channels are the dearest of all.</text><text x='36' y='186' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='9.5' letter-spacing='1.5' fill='#3D5560'>AND FROM JANUARY 2026</text><rect x='36' y='198' width='340' height='86' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='49' y='222' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#993C1D'>A one per cent United States excise</text><text x='49' y='243' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>It applies to cash based remittances, which is</text><text x='49' y='258' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>nudging even the senders loyal to the counter</text><text x='49' y='273' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>toward their phones.</text><rect x='396' y='198' width='328' height='86' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='409' y='222' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#0E4D5C'>Where the comparison happens now</text><text x='409' y='243' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>SendMoneyPacific, the Pacific's own site, closed in</text><text x='409' y='258' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>2026. Remittance Prices Worldwide is the standing</text><text x='409' y='273' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>reference for the question every group chat asks.</text><line x1='36' y1='302' x2='724' y2='302' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='380' y='324' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#3D5560'>Six per cent on 200 dollars is 12 dollars. The target would make it 6.</text></svg>",
    "figcap": "What it costs to send 200 US dollars home against the global target. From World Bank Remittance Prices Worldwide, third quarter 2025, and the IRS on the new excise.",
    "teaser": "Which app, whose promotional rate, who still queues at the agent on Saturday: diaspora group chats trade fee advice constantly, because sending 200 dollars home still costs about 6 percent, and a new US tax on cash transfers is pushing the talk toward phones.",
    "body": "Ask any diaspora group chat and the fee talk starts immediately: which app is cheapest this month, whose promotional rate is about to expire, who still queues at an agent on a Saturday because grandma trusts the counter. Public comparison sites are built for exactly this conversation, and the Pacific's own, SendMoneyPacific, closed in 2026, leaving the World Bank's Remittance Prices Worldwide as the standing reference. Sending 200 US dollars home still costs about 6 percent on average, double the global target, with cash and bank channels the dearest of all, and a new 1 percent US excise on cash based remittances from January 2026 is nudging even the loyal toward their phones.",
