    "fig": "<svg viewBox='0 0 760 446' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' role='img' aria-label='Money flows from Marseille to Grande Comore to fund the grand mariage, and four public voices argue over whether it should.'><rect width='760' height='446' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='36' y='34' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='9.5' letter-spacing='1.5' fill='#3D5560'>THE FLOW THAT FUNDS IT</text><rect x='36' y='48' width='200' height='56' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' fill-opacity='1' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='136.0' y='80.0' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0B2530'>Marseille</text><rect x='300' y='48' width='160' height='56' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' fill-opacity='1' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='380.0' y='80.0' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0B2530'>Grande Comore</text><rect x='524' y='48' width='200' height='56' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' fill-opacity='1' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='624.0' y='80.0' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12' fill='#0B2530'>The grand mariage</text><line x1='244' y1='76' x2='284' y2='76' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='2.2'/><polygon points='283,71 292,76 283,81' fill='#0E4D5C'/><line x1='468' y1='76' x2='508' y2='76' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='2.2'/><polygon points='507,71 516,76 507,81' fill='#993C1D'/><text x='36' y='128' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>The largest Comorian community outside the islands sends back more than any donor does. The ceremony secures full</text><text x='36' y='143' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>social standing and can cost the equivalent of tens of thousands of euros.</text><text x='36' y='182' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='9.5' letter-spacing='1.5' fill='#3D5560'>THE ARGUMENT, FULLY PUBLIC AND FULLY COMORIAN</text><rect x='36' y='194' width='336' height='84' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='49' y='218' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#0E4D5C'>Community news sites</text><text x='49' y='239' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>Reportage on weddings that sell for auction level</text><text x='49' y='254' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>sums in France.</text><rect x='388' y='194' width='336' height='84' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='401' y='218' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#0E4D5C'>Comorian magazines</text><text x='401' y='239' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>Tradition and prestige weighed against</text><text x='401' y='254' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>contemporary costs.</text><rect x='36' y='290' width='336' height='84' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='49' y='314' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#993C1D'>Younger diaspora voices</text><text x='49' y='335' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>They ask openly whether that wealth should go into</text><text x='49' y='350' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>productive investment instead.</text><rect x='388' y='290' width='336' height='84' rx='5' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='401' y='314' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#993C1D'>Those who defend the anda</text><text x='401' y='335' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>They call it the social infrastructure that binds</text><text x='401' y='350' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0B2530'>the diaspora to home.</text><line x1='36' y1='394' x2='724' y2='394' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='380' y='416' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#3D5560'>Money flows back to Grande Comore on a scale beyond what any donor sends.</text></svg>",
    "figcap": "The flow, and the four voices arguing over it. From Comorian community news sites, magazines and diaspora commentary.",
    "teaser": "From Marseille, money flows back to Grande Comore at a scale beyond what any donor sends, much of it toward the grand mariage, and a generational debate in the Comorian press and diaspora asks whether that wealth should build something else.",
    "body": "From Marseille, home to the largest Comorian community outside the islands, money flows back to Grande Comore on a scale beyond what any donor sends, and much of it funds the grand mariage, the customary marriage that secures full social standing and can cost the equivalent of tens of thousands of euros. The debate is fully public and fully Comorian: community news sites run reportage on weddings that sell for auction level sums in France, Comorian magazines weigh tradition and prestige against contemporary costs, and younger voices in the diaspora ask openly whether that wealth should go into productive investment instead, while others defend the anda as the social infrastructure that binds the diaspora to home.",
